# Dataset Description

## Airport Dataset

The airport dataset was collected from the OurAirports website.

It contains information about airports around the world such as:
- Airport name
- Country
- Latitude and longitude
- Airport type
- Elevation

The following files were used:
- airports.csv
- countries.csv
- regions.csv

---

## Flight Delay Dataset

The flight delay dataset contains information about flights and delays.

The dataset includes:
- Flight information
- Airport codes
- Airline information
- Delay data

The dataset will later be used for preprocessing, analysis, and prediction.

---

## Why these countries were selected

I selected the following countries/regions from the dataset:

- United States (US)
- Puerto Rico (PR)
- Papua New Guinea (PG)
- Namibia (NA)
- Europe (EU)

These were chosen because they are the only available values in the `iso_country` column of the dataset.

Using only countries that exist in the dataset ensures:
- No missing or invalid filters occur during data processing
- The analysis is fully consistent with the available data
- The results are reproducible without errors

Additionally, these selections provide a mix of different geographic regions, which helps give a more diverse view of the airport data.

Note: "Europe (EU)" appears as a region code in the dataset rather than a single country, but it is included because it exists as a valid category in the data.
import pandas as pd

airports = pd.read_csv("airports.csv")
countries = pd.read_csv("countries.csv")
regions = pd.read_csv("regions.csv")

delays = pd.read_csv("flight_delays.csv")

print("Airports Dataset")
print(airports.head())

print("\nFlight Delays Dataset")
print(delays.head())

print("\nAirports Info")
print(airports.info())

print("\nDelays Info")
print(delays.info())

print("\nMissing Values in Airports")
print(airports.isnull().sum())

print("\nMissing Values in Delays")
print(delays.isnull().sum())

selected_countries = ['US', 'PR', 'PG', 'NA', 'EU']

filtered_airports = airports[
    airports['iso_country'].isin(selected_countries)
]

print("\nSelected Countries")
print(filtered_airports['iso_country'].value_counts())

filtered_airports.to_csv(
    "filtered_airports.csv",
    index=False
)

print("\nFiltered dataset saved successfully.")



